{"skill":{"slug":"qmd","displayName":"Qmd"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545374981,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":817,"sha256":"8d0a688885a61062a655259d755d050e5a51a54d80fe1c1643756bf0dbba41cf","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1702,"sha256":"bb45f43d27e8c6647ca038ea6eecc891a9b7fb6c8cd256c39d456637444ab464","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013742169,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"aa852ef1ed901736d738def596441e12a68bf181f76f11f4659e2fbda259bb4f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/aa852ef1ed901736d738def596441e12a68bf181f76f11f4659e2fbda259bb4f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: qmd\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle defines a local search/indexing CLI tool. The `SKILL.md` provides installation instructions for `qmd` from a seemingly legitimate GitHub repository (`https://github.com/tobi/qmd`) and outlines local CLI usage. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution instructions, persistence mechanisms, prompt injection attempts, or obfuscation. All described operations are local and aligned with the stated purpose of a search/indexing tool.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159623316},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789013742169},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward local file indexing/search helper, with a real but disclosed install supply-chain risk from an unpinned GitHub dependency.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Local file indexing and a cache under ~/.cache/qmd are proportionate to a local search tool, but users should choose indexed paths carefully because selected file contents may be stored in the index.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The metadata installs the qmd executable from a mutable GitHub repository URL rather than a pinned revision or checksummed release, creating a supply-chain risk but not artifact-backed malicious behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The runtime instructions are concise and user-directed; they do not ask the agent to override policy, hide behavior, exfiltrate data, or automatically index broad locations without user-specified paths.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill discloses persistent index storage under ~/.cache/qmd and does not request elevated privileges, scheduled tasks, hooks, or background persistence.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to index local files and search them using qmd, and the instructions only describe qmd indexing, search, retrieval, status, and MCP mode.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable running qmd from its GitHub source. Prefer a pinned commit or reviewed release if available, and only add collections for directories whose contents you intend to make searchable and cached locally.","findings":"[T08] unexpected: The unpinned GitHub install source is a valid supply-chain concern, but the artifact does not show malicious dependency behavior, hidden execution, or privilege escalation; this is best handled as install guidance rather than a Review verdict.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013742169}}}}}